SUMMARY:CRA Special Call Meeting
LOCATION:Tampa \, FL United States
DESCRIPTION:NOTICE OF PUBLIC MEETING CITY OF TAMPA COMMUNITY REDEVELOPMENT
  AGENCY SPECIAL CALL PUBLIC MEETING Date: Thursday\, August 27\, 2026 Time
 : 10:00 A.M. Location: City Council Chambers\, Old City Hall 315 E. Kenned
 y Blvd. Tampa FL 33602 Agenda: The Board may discuss\, act on\, or provide
  direction to staff and counsel regarding the draft agreements between the
  Tampa Bay Rays\, Hillsborough County\, the City of Tampa\, and the Commun
 ity Redevelopment Agency of the City of Tampa\, Florida (the CRA)\, includ
 ing the draft Stadium and Development Agreement and all related draft agre
 ements\, instruments\, resolutions and documents. The CRA Board may take a
 ny and all action permitted by law with respect to the foregoing\, includi
 ng\, without limitation: approving\, approving with conditions\, modifying
 \, disapproving\, deferring\, or continuing consideration of the draft agr
 eements\\\; adopting resolutions\\\; making findings and determinations\\\
 ; authorizing and directing the execution and delivery of documents\\\; an
 d providing direction to CRA staff and counsel. Final action may be taken 
 at this meeting. Copies of the agenda and any available backup materials m
 ay be obtained as follows: Please contact Cedric McCray at (813) 274-3284 
 or at Cedric.McCraytampagov.net. Purpose: The purpose of this special call
  meeting is for the CRA Board to consider\, discuss\, act upon\, and provi
 de direction to staff and counsel regarding the draft Stadium and Developm
 ent Agreement\, and related draft agreements\, by and among the Tampa Bay 
 Rays Company\, LLC\, Hillsborough County\, Florida\, the City of Tampa\, F
 lorida\, and the CRA\, including any participation\, funding\, pledge of t
 ax increment revenues\, or other undertaking by the CRA contemplated there
 by. This special call meeting was called by a vote of the CRA Board taken 
 at its publicly noticed meeting held on August 20\, 2026\, upon the reques
 t of CRA Board member Bill Carlson\, pursuant to Article II\, Section 3 of
  the By-Laws of the CRA. Notice of this meeting is given by the Secretary 
 of the CRA in accordance with Article II\, Section 3 of the By-Laws and ap
 plicable law. Pursuant to Article III of the By-Laws\, all actions of the 
 CRA shall be adopted by an affirmative vote of not fewer than four (4) mem
 bers of the CRA unless otherwise specified in the By-Laws. The public and 
 citizens of the City of Tampa will be able to watch\, listen to\, or view 
 this meeting on: Cable TV: Spectrum Channel 640 Frontier Channel 15 Intern
 et: https:www.tampa.govlivestream (https:www.tampa.govlivestream) Members 
 of the public can attend in person in City Council chambers in Old City Ha
 ll or virtually participate in this public meeting by using what is referr
 ed to by State of Florida statutes and rules as communications media techn
 ology (CMT). In accordance with Section 286.0114\, Florida Statutes\, Arti
 cle II\, Section 4 of the By-Laws of the CRA\, and the Rules of Procedure 
 of the Tampa City Council\, members of the public shall be given a reasona
 ble opportunity to be heard on propositions before the CRA Board before th
 e CRA Board takes official action. TO SPEAK REMOTELY DURING PUBLIC COMMENT
  WITH THE USE OF CMT PRE-REGISTRATION IS REQUIRED : Complete the form at h
 ttps:www.tampa.govPublicComment AND state on the form under Request Type t
 hat you wish to speak live during the public comment period. You will then
  be contacted with additional instructions on how to participate live thro
 ugh the use of CMT. Registration for speaking remotely must be requested a
 t least 24 hours prior to the meeting. In accordance with the Americans wi
 th Disabilities Act (ADA) and Section 286.26\, Florida Statutes\, persons 
 with disabilities needing a reasonable accommodation to participate in thi
 s public hearing or meeting should contact the City of Tampas ADA Coordina
 tor at least 48 hours prior to the proceeding. The ADA Coordinator may be 
 contacted via phone at 813-274-3964\, email at TampaADAtampagov.net\, or b
 y submitting an ADA - Accommodations Request form available online at tamp
 agov.netADARequest. In accordance with Section 286.0105\, Florida Statutes
 \, any person who decides to appeal any decision made by the CRA Board wit
 h respect to any matter considered at this meeting will need a record of t
 he proceedings\, and for such purpose may need to ensure that a verbatim r
 ecord of the proceedings is made\, which record includes the testimony and
  evidence upon which the appeal is to be based. One or more members of the
  Tampa City Council\, of the CRA Board\, of the CRAs Community Advisory Co
 mmittees\, andor of other boards\, committees or agencies of the City of T
 ampa may be present at this meeting. \n\nPermalink: https://www.tampa.gov/
 node/193921
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/193921
