DTEND:20260924T000000Z
SUMMARY:David Hockney: Perspective Should Be Reversed Opening Celebration
LOCATION:120 W. Gasparilla Plaza Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:Be among the first to explore the Tampa Museum of Arts newest 
 contemporary exhibition David Hockney: Perspective Should Be Reversed. Joi
 n us for a Curators Chat with Joanna Robotham\, Curator of Modern and Cont
 emporary Art\, as we learn more about one of the most influential and belo
 ved artists of the 20th and 21st centuries. Programming\, gallery access\,
  light bites\, and access to a cash bar included with purchase. David Hock
 ney: Perspective Should Be Reversed presents 60 years of work by acclaimed
  British artist David Hockney (19372026). Drawn from the collections of th
 e Jordan D. Schnitzer and His Family Foundation\, the exhibition features 
 over 140 prints\, collages\, photographs\, and iPad drawings. A comprehens
 ive survey of Hockneys groundbreaking explorations in printmaking\, video\
 , and new media\, Perspective Should Be Reversed highlights the artists si
 gnature motifs. Intimate portraits of friends and family\, bucolic landsca
 pes\, Los Angeles swimming pools\, vibrant interior spaces\, and stage des
 igns present a unique glimpse into Hockneys visual world. \n\nPermalink: h
 ttps://www.tampa.gov/node/193851
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/193851
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0cc1f770-8fe1-417b-b0ef-194a33dee6e0
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260830T000710Z
DTSTART:20260924T160000Z
DTEND:20260924T200000Z
SUMMARY:Remember. Rebuild. Prepare. - Hurricane Preparedness Kit Day 2026
LOCATION:402 w laurel st Tampa \, FL 33607 United States
DESCRIPTION:Two years after the 2024 hurricanes\, many Florida families ar
 e still rebuilding\, while communities across Greater Tampa Bay continue p
 reparing for future storms. On Thursday\, September 24\, 2026\, Hurricane 
 Help Florida and StormResQ will host the inaugural Remember. Rebuild. Prep
 are. event at the Bob Buckhorn River Center. The event will bring resident
 s together with trusted disaster-recovery organizations\, local contractor
 s and community resources while raising awareness and support for families
  still living in damaged homes. The event is free and open to the public f
 rom 2:00 to 4:00 p.m. Hurricane Help Florida will distribute 500 resident 
 hurricane-preparedness kits and 250 pet-preparedness kits while supplies l
 ast. Guests may also make a 45 donation to attend from 12:00 to 2:00 p.m.\
 , which includes lunch from SaltBlock Hospitality and helps support contin
 ued rebuilding efforts. We are honored to welcome John Bennett\, Chief of 
 Staff for the City of Tampa\, along with nonprofit partners\, volunteers\,
  community leaders and local businesses committed to strengthening Greater
  Tampa Bays disaster preparedness and long-term recovery. You can register
  to attend at: Remember. Rebuild. Prepare \n\nPermalink: https://www.tampa
 .gov/node/193986
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/193986
END:VEVENT
